[272.853459, "i", "encore --help\n"]
[272.853633, "o", "encore --help\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[272.878452, "o", "encore is the fastest way of developing backend applications\r\n\r\n"]
[272.878498, "o", "Usage:\r\n  encore [command]\r\n\r\nAvailable Commands:\r\n  app                             Commands to create and link Encore apps\r\n  auth                            Commands to authenticate with Encore\r\n  build                           build provides ways to build your application for deployment\r\n  check                           Runs a list of HTTP requests against a fresh app instance\r\n  config                          Get or set a configuration value\r\n  daemon                          Starts the encore daemon\r\n  db                              Database management commands\r\n  exec                            Runs executable scripts against the local Encore app\r\n  gen                             Code generation commands\r\n  help                            Help about any command\r\n  kubernetes                      Kubernetes management commands\r\n  llm-rules                       Commands to create LLM rules for apps\r\n  logs                            Streams logs from your application\r\n  mcp                             MCP (Message Context Provider) commands\r\n  namespace                       Manage infrastructure namespaces\r\n  rand                            Utilities for generating cryptographically secure random data\r\n  run                             Runs your application\r\n  secret                          Secret management commands\r\n  telemetry                       Reports the current telemetry status\r\n  test                            Tests your application\r\n  version                         Reports the current version of the encore application\r\n\r\nFlags:\r\n  -h, --help            help for encore\r\n      --trace string    file to write execution trace data to\r\n  -v, --verbose count   verbose output\r\n\r\nUse \"encore [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\r\n"]
[272.881948, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@98cbecab-966c-4aeb-9947-03f45a20a13e:/home/user/myproject# "]
[276.63748, "i", "encore gen --help\n"]
[276.637653, "o", "encore gen --help\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[276.662246, "o", "Code generation commands\r\n\r\nUsage:\r\n  encore gen [command]\r\n\r\nAvailable Commands:\r\n  client      Generates an API client for your app\r\n  wrappers    Generates user-facing wrapper code\r\n\r\nFlags:\r\n  -h, --help   help for gen\r\n\r\nGlobal Flags:\r\n      --trace string    file to write execution trace data to\r\n  -v, --verbose count   verbose output\r\n\r\nUse \"encore gen [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\r\n"]
[276.66571, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@98cbecab-966c-4aeb-9947-03f45a20a13e:/home/user/myproject# "]
[277.606758, "i", "encore build --help\n"]
[277.606975, "o", "encore build --help\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[277.631059, "o", "build provides ways to build your application for deployment\r\n\r\nUsage:\r\n  encore build [command]\r\n\r\nAliases:\r\n  build, eject\r\n\r\nAvailable Commands:\r\n  docker      docker builds a portable docker image of your Encore application\r\n\r\nFlags:\r\n  -h, --help   help for build\r\n\r\nGlobal Flags:\r\n      --trace string    file to write execution trace data to\r\n  -v, --verbose count   verbose output\r\n\r\nUse \"encore build [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\r\n"]
[277.634787, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@98cbecab-966c-4aeb-9947-03f45a20a13e:/home/user/myproject# "]
[281.578717, "i", "encore gen wrappers --help\n"]
[281.578907, "o", "encore gen wrappers --help\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[281.606725, "o", "Manually regenerates user-facing wrapper code.\r\n\r\nThis is typically not something you ever need to call during regular development,\r\nas Encore REDACTEDmatically regenerates the wrappers whenever the code-base changes.\r\n\r\nIts core use case is for CI/CD workflows where you want to run custom linters,\r\nwhich may require the user-facing wrapper code to be manually generated.\r\n\r\nUsage:\r\n  encore gen wrappers [flags]\r\n\r\nFlags:\r\n  -h, --help   help for wrappers\r\n\r\nGlobal Flags:\r\n      --trace string    file to write execution trace data to\r\n  -v, --verbose count   verbose output\r\n"]
[281.610373, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@98cbecab-966c-4aeb-9947-03f45a20a13e:/home/user/myproject# "]
[285.324854, "i", "encore gen wrappers\n"]
